%U A398617 2,9,8,8,4,9,3,9,4,0,6,3,6,6,9,5,8,7,4,8,0,9
%N A398617 Decimal expansion of the large face angle, in radians, of a canonical (dual-uniform) 9-gonal trapezohedron.
%C A398617 The 9-gonal trapezohedron is the dual polyhedron of the 9-gonal antiprism.
%C A398617 Its faces are kites with one acute angle (A398616) and three obtuse angles (this constant).
%H A398617 Paolo Xausa, <a href="/A398617/b398617.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%H A398617 Polytope Wiki, <a href="https://polytope.miraheze.org/wiki/Enneagonal_antitegum">Enneagonal antitegum</a>.
%H A398617 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/Trapezohedron.html">Trapezohedron</a>.
%F A398617 Equals arccos(1/2 - cos(Pi/9)) = arccos(1/2 - A019879).
%F A398617 Equals arccos(c), where c = -0.43969... is the smallest root of 8*x^3 - 12*x^2 + 3.
%e A398617 2.026052734923053894418295296399715646244684383893...
%t A398617 First[RealDigits[ArcCos[1/2 - Cos[Pi/9]], 10, 100]]
%Y A398617 Cf. A398610 (volume), A398611 (surface area), A398612 (inradius), A398613 (midradius), A398614 (height).
%Y A398617 Cf. A398615 (long edge).
%Y A398617 Cf. A398616 (small face angle), A398618 (dihedral angle).
%Y A398617 Cf. A019879.
